{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"reviewThreads":{"nodes":[{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y2h8-","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"packages/daemon/src/shadow-sync.ts","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This relative import is not valid in the built daemon layout. `build:daemon` copies this file to `dist/daemon/shadow-sync.ts`, so `../../parser/shadow.js` resolves to `parser/shadow.js` at repo root instead of `dist/parser/shadow.js`. That makes daemon startup fail on the packaged/runtime path, which matches the red smoke CI.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901701222"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y2h9A","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"packages/daemon/src/server.ts","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: Same runtime path problem here. From `dist/daemon/server.ts`, `../../parser/config.js` resolves outside `dist`, so the daemon cannot load project config during startup. The current PR head already shows this as `e2e (playwright smoke)` failing with `Daemon failed to start within 5 seconds`.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901701224"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3JBJ","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"src/parser/shadow.ts","line":1469,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This PR covers write-side sync, but the task description also requires pulling fresh shadow state before CLI read operations such as `task list` and similar read paths. Those code paths are unchanged in this branch, so a second clone can still read stale task/spec state until manual `kspec shadow sync` or the daemon interval happens to run.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901902216"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3N45","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"src/parser/yaml.ts","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This pre-read sync path drops the resolved shadow config. `hasRemoteTracking(specDir)` and `shadowPull(specDir)` fall back to `kspec-meta`/`origin`, so custom `shadow.branch` or `shadow.remote` setups silently skip sync or use the wrong upstream. Pass the resolved shadow options through here.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901926252"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3N47","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"tests/shadow-sync-scheduler.test.ts","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This file copies `ShadowSyncScheduler` instead of importing the production class, so `@config-shadow ac-12` is not actually covered on the shipped daemon code path. A regression in `packages/daemon/src/shadow-sync.ts` could pass this suite unchanged.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901926254"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3N9-","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":true,"path":"src/parser/shadow.ts","line":null,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: `remoteBranchExists(projectRoot, branchName)` still defaults to `origin`. That breaks the new bidirectional sync flow for configured remotes (`shadow.remote` named/path/url), which is already part of `@config-shadow`. This lookup needs to follow the branch's configured upstream, not hardcode the default.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901926615"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3Shq","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"src/parser/yaml.ts","line":404,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: this new CLI pre-read path now depends on `shadowPull(specDir, shadowOpts)`, but `shadowPull()` still does its remote-branch existence precheck against the default `origin`. I reproduced that on this head with `shadow.remote: specs-origin`: the call returned `{ success: true, pulled: false }` and did not pull the file pushed to `specs-origin`, so `task list` / `session start` can still read stale state in multi-clone setups with a non-`origin` shadow remote.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901949242"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3Sht","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"src/parser/shadow-sync-scheduler.ts","line":104,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: the daemon scheduler reuses the same `shadowPull()` path, so it inherits the configured-remote bug above. For named remotes other than `origin` (and path/URL remotes routed through `kspec-specs`), `syncOnce()` can report success without ever pulling the remote shadow updates that AC-12 is supposed to surface locally.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901949246"}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDOQ7Tfmc5y3Shv","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":"tests/shadow.test.ts","line":1219,"comments":{"nodes":[{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: this new pre-read coverage only exercises the default `origin` flow. There still isn’t a regression test for the configured-remote case (`shadow.remote: specs-origin` or path/URL remotes routed through `kspec-specs`), which is why the `shadowPull()` bug above slipped through even after the previous fix cycle.","url":"https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/712#discussion_r2901949248"}]}}]}}}}}
